WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.533 --> 00:00:03.566
Jocelyn Tyson,

00:00:03.566 --> 00:00:05.400
"Have You Been There?"

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.766
"Have You Been There?"

00:00:06.766 --> 00:00:16.600
Jocelyn Tyson.

00:00:16.666 --> 00:00:17.066
Thank you,

00:00:17.066 --> 00:00:18.400
Contest Chair.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.133
You're welcome.

00:00:22.233 --> 00:00:26.966
It was the summer of 2021,
and I was reaching a milestone birthday.

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:31.166
I decided to skip the party and pick
something epic off my bucket list:

00:00:31.233 --> 00:00:33.966
Triathlon.

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:35.733
For those of you unfamiliar, it is a race

00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:39.666
that contains three disciplines:
Swim, bike, run.

00:00:39.733 --> 00:00:44.966
Now, almost immediately, my inner
go-getter said, "Yeah, let's do this! Show 'em

00:00:44.966 --> 00:00:48.466
you still got it."

00:00:48.566 --> 00:00:50.266
But my inner critic:

00:00:50.266 --> 00:00:52.400
"Slow down, hot stuff.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.700
You hate swimming.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.600
You barely bike, and girl,

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:58.133
wait a minute,

00:00:58.133 --> 00:00:58.833
that swimming thing,

00:00:58.833 --> 00:01:01.833
you can't do it!"

00:01:02.066 --> 00:01:05.266
And just like that,
I had two warring sides,

00:01:05.366 --> 00:01:10.233
both with logical explanations
for why I should or shouldn't do it.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:13.300
A decision to make. This one, yes.

00:01:13.533 --> 00:01:18.200
That one, no. Have you been there?

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.300
I decided to go with my inner go-getter.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.766
I signed up for the race.
I started jogging,

00:01:23.766 --> 00:01:25.566
I borrowed a bike, and yes, friends,

00:01:25.566 --> 00:01:27.900
I took swim lessons.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:31.600
And after eight months straight
of training every day,

00:01:31.666 --> 00:01:33.766
I was ready.

00:01:33.766 --> 00:01:35.200
It's race day.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.733
People are lined up along the banks

00:01:36.733 --> 00:01:40.566
of a lake, ready
to start the first part, the swim.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:44.533
They blow the whistle and the race is off.

00:01:44.633 --> 00:01:47.133
I, on the other hand,
am still at the bank

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:49.966
of the lake. Why?

00:01:49.966 --> 00:01:50.933
You see, friends,

00:01:50.933 --> 00:01:54.666
my brain cannot seem to understand
that the water, the dark,

00:01:54.666 --> 00:01:59.933
dreary, cedar water, was the same water
that I had learned to swim in at the pool.

00:02:00.033 --> 00:02:01.866
There it was clear,
you could see to the bottom.

00:02:01.866 --> 00:02:04.833
But this, this was darkness.

00:02:04.833 --> 00:02:08.700
I go to put my face in
and I couldn't do it.

00:02:08.766 --> 00:02:10.533
I couldn't do it.

00:02:10.533 --> 00:02:13.800
I started to panic.

00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:14.766
I look over to my right.

00:02:14.766 --> 00:02:17.733
I see my family.
They're looking back at me. What's wrong?

00:02:17.733 --> 00:02:18.933
I look over to the other side and

00:02:18.933 --> 00:02:21.433
I can see all the people lined up
to see the start of the race.

00:02:21.433 --> 00:02:22.366
They're watching me.

00:02:22.366 --> 00:02:25.366
And behind me are the people coming up
for their next wave of the swim.

00:02:25.533 --> 00:02:28.233
I had a choice
to make. Go forward into the water

00:02:28.233 --> 00:02:28.866
or go back home

00:02:28.866 --> 00:02:31.300
from where I came.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.166
A situation.

00:02:33.166 --> 00:02:33.633
This one,

00:02:33.633 --> 00:02:36.300
yes. That one, no.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.900
Have you been there?

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:41.800
I chose to do the only thing any would do
with that logical situation.

00:02:41.866 --> 00:02:48.100
I flipped over on my back
and started the backstroke.

00:02:48.166 --> 00:02:50.866
Now, swimming

00:02:50.866 --> 00:02:54.866
has a certain grace, a beauty,
if you will.

00:02:54.933 --> 00:02:57.700
This had neither grace nor beauty.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:02:59.333
This was not swimming.

00:02:59.333 --> 00:03:02.266
This was surviving.

00:03:02.266 --> 00:03:03.933
I'm knocking into people,
bumping into things,

00:03:03.933 --> 00:03:05.100
knocking things over 

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:09.866
and around, all things going on, all the while
hyperventilating before I realize

00:03:09.933 --> 00:03:11.833
I heard it.

00:03:11.933 --> 00:03:18.333
"Ma'am, you're going the wrong way!"

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.866
All I could think to myself
at that time was,

00:03:20.866 --> 00:03:24.633
I wonder who they're talking to.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:25.900
"Ma'am,

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:30.333
322, you're going the wrong way."

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:33.033
322. No, no, I'm 322.

00:03:33.033 --> 00:03:33.800
I look over.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.833
I am 50 meters off course.

00:03:35.833 --> 00:03:37.833
Now in swim time that's not too bad,

00:03:37.833 --> 00:03:40.233
but for me, it was everything.

00:03:40.233 --> 00:03:42.033
I had to stop, get myself together,

00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:43.600
and I got back on course.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:46.833
Now, there are lifeguards spread out along
the lake in canoes.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.800
I swim up to one of the canoes.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:50.433
The lifeguard, she looks over the boat.

00:03:50.433 --> 00:03:55.066
She looks at me and says, "Ma'am,
you really need to think this through,

00:03:55.066 --> 00:03:57.666
okay? Look, you can still finish the race.

00:03:57.666 --> 00:03:59.900
We'll let you finish the bike.
We'll let you finish the run.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:03.333
But you might want
to think about quitting this."

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.800
And I understood where she was
coming from.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:08.033
There was a lot going on.

00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:11.033
My inner critic agreed with her
all the more.

00:04:11.266 --> 00:04:13.433
"You're in over your head,

00:04:13.433 --> 00:04:16.433
like 12 feet to be exact.

00:04:16.533 --> 00:04:19.533
Quitting
sounds like a smart move right now."

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:22.400
I looked up at her. I let go.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.800
I kept on swimming.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:28.700
I went on for another few more meters
before I grabbed hold of another canoe.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:33.266
That lifeguard leaned over
and she said to me, "You're doing good.

00:04:33.366 --> 00:04:35.100
Not much further.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:38.600
You got this."

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:40.533
Advice.

00:04:40.533 --> 00:04:42.033
This one, yes.

00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:43.800
That one, no.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:47.533
Have you been there?

00:04:47.633 --> 00:04:48.633
I let go.

00:04:48.633 --> 00:04:50.233
I finished the swim.

00:04:50.233 --> 00:04:53.000
I'm staggering up the bank. My legs
feel like lead.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.933
My lungs are on fire.

00:04:54.933 --> 00:04:58.166
I'm coughing out water,
all the while exhausted.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.266
I get to the bike.
I fall up on top of the bike,

00:05:01.266 --> 00:05:04.200
one foot in front of the other as I pedal.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:08.266
To this day, I have no clue how I finished
those 12 miles, but I got them done.

00:05:08.366 --> 00:05:12.133
When I finished,
I tossed the bike to the side.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.266
I have now the run to do.

00:05:14.266 --> 00:05:18.000
At this point, my inner critic steps out
bold and says,

00:05:18.166 --> 00:05:21.066
"You still have a third to do?

00:05:21.066 --> 00:05:23.033
You hate running.

00:05:23.033 --> 00:05:27.733
Why are we still here?"

00:05:27.833 --> 00:05:29.066
At this point, my inner

00:05:29.066 --> 00:05:32.066
go-getter steps out and says,

00:05:32.066 --> 00:05:34.100
"We only have a third left to do.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.266
You trained for this. Yes!

00:05:36.266 --> 00:05:39.900
Yes! We're still here."

00:05:39.966 --> 00:05:42.666
I shimmy, shod, struggle, trouble,

00:05:42.666 --> 00:05:47.366
stanky legs all the way across to clear
that finish line.

00:05:47.433 --> 00:05:50.433
I had done what I intended.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.233
That race took a lot out of me,

00:05:53.233 --> 00:05:56.766
but I took more out of it.

00:05:56.833 --> 00:05:59.833
Whether you have to make a big decision,

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.000
overcome a situation, take advice,

00:06:03.033 --> 00:06:06.033
or just finish what you started.

00:06:06.233 --> 00:06:09.133
These are things that can happen in life,

00:06:09.133 --> 00:06:12.300
can have two warring sides. This one,

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:14.700
yes. That one, no.

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:16.833
And both can come
with logical explanations

00:06:16.833 --> 00:06:18.933
on what you should or shouldn't do it.

00:06:18.933 --> 00:06:20.900
Do I start a new job?

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:22.866
Do I begin chemo?

00:06:22.866 --> 00:06:24.200
Do I finish chemo?

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:27.633
Do I move? Do I start a new family?

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:30.700
Whether
you think you can or you think you can't.

00:06:30.933 --> 00:06:32.433
You're right.

00:06:32.433 --> 00:06:34.800
It was said by Henry Ford,

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:39.466
"Because what matters most is
what is within you." Friends,

00:06:39.533 --> 00:06:42.400
you can be your worst critic.

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:46.000
No one knows your weaknesses
or your flaws like you do.

00:06:46.066 --> 00:06:48.600
But at the same time,
you can be your biggest cheerleader,

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:52.033
and no one can push you further
or take you higher.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:57.366
I implore you, no, I beg you,
look deep within on that next challenge.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:58.733
Find your inner

00:06:58.733 --> 00:07:00.433
go-getter

00:07:00.433 --> 00:07:03.166
and see how far it can push you.

00:07:03.166 --> 00:07:04.533
I've been there.

00:07:04.533 --> 00:07:06.600
Have you? Contest Chair. 

